# Wonder Wands (windurst 48): Hakkuru-Rinkuru (Port Windurst; +7: the first of the name is cutscene-only; default action
# 224; once Making Amends is completed its container answers him with 281 (replaceDefault, no mustZone), which takes
# turns with his script; while it is accepted, its 275; a script talk that starts nothing plays the container's event
# again), Goltata and Yaman-Hachuman (no default; their standards 232 / 233 in their scripts). A level-75 WAR, Making
# Amends and Making Amens! completed by GMs (no mustZone). Available: Goltata 232, Yaman-Hachuman 233; fame level 4:
# nothing; the three traded: nothing (not accepted). Level 5 with needToZone (a GM's flag): nothing; rezoned. Making
# Amends accepted (GM): nothing; Making Amens! accepted (GM): nothing. Both completed: 259, option 0: nothing; option 1:
# begun. Accepted: 260; two of the three traded: 260 (0, 17091, 17061, 17053); three items with one of the three missing
# (each in turn): 260; the three and a fourth item: 260; Goltata 257 (0, 0, 17091), Yaman-Hachuman 256 (0, 0, 0, 17061).
# No free slot, the three alone: 265; its finish: ITEM_CANNOT_BE_OBTAINED only, SecondRewardVar not set (user ruling
# 2026-11-04, kept Lua bugs: the Lua's trade set it before 265, whatever the space). The trigger: 260. One free slot
# (inventory 31), the three: 265: SecondRewardVar 1, the trade taken, 4800 gil, the New Moon Armlets, fame 50, the
# title, completed. Completed, SecondRewardVar 1: 267: two of the three back by the roll (here 1:
# the staff and the rod), var 0; then nothing; the trade: nothing; Goltata 269, Yaman-Hachuman 268.
